+# Privacy engineering and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed 2026-11-06. Scope: all supplied HTML, CSS, package metadata, and the publish configuration. This is a source-level audit; it is not an assessment of a live host or of services linked by the original navigation.
+
+## Data minimization and client behavior
+
+The site is informational. There are no forms, scripts, analytics, cookies, browser storage, identifiers, fingerprinting, geolocation requests, or client-side network APIs. No consent banner is needed for the functionality implemented here. Keep browsing available without an account. The privacy link now resolves to a local notice explaining this scope and the hosting boundary.
+
+The hero originally fetched an image from images.unsplash.com on every visit, exposing visitor network information to that provider. The same image is now stored at assets/coffee.jpg. System fonts and a local stylesheet eliminate other resource dependencies. Inline styles were extracted so the Content Security Policy can prohibit inline code. There are no client scripts to sanitize or retain: script execution, workers, frames, form submissions, and outbound script connections are denied by policy. Ordinary link navigation remains available.
+
+The unconditional GET /logout link was removed: this static site has no authenticated session, and a future logout must use a server-side POST with CSRF protection rather than a state-changing GET.
+
+## Third-party inventory
+
+| Component | Visitor data exposure | Disposition |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash coffee photograph | Previously received each visitor's image request | Downloaded once during implementation; now served locally. Original source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085. Review applicable image licensing when reusing assets. |
+| Fonts, analytics, ads, embeds, SDKs | None in supplied source | No external assets, runtime libraries, or tracking providers permitted. |
+| Website host/CDN | Necessarily receives IP addresses, request paths, and request metadata | Provider is not specified in this repository. Operator must review logging, access, retention, subprocessors, and regional settings before production. |
+| Node build and test tools | No visitor data | Uses only Node built-ins; no installed production or build dependencies. |
+| Existing `pnpm dlx statikk` start command | Development tooling, not shipped client code | Downloads an unpinned external tool when invoked. Not run or independently audited here; do not use it as the production security boundary. |
+
+Review this inventory when adding a dependency or external resource and before each release. Record provider, purpose, fields disclosed, necessity, retention, subprocessors, and deletion options. Prefer local assets and avoid sending request URLs or identifiers to telemetry/reporting services. Do not add host-injected analytics or tracking snippets without updating the audit, notice, and policy.
+
+## Security headers and deployment
+
+`npm run build` creates an allowlisted `dist/` containing only the pages, assets, and `_headers`. `npm test` checks privacy invariants and header parity without a browser or server. Deploy `dist/` to a static HTTPS host:
+
+- Netlify or Cloudflare Pages: `_headers` supplies the response headers for every path. Use the build command and publish directory above.
+- Vercel: root `vercel.json` sets the build, output directory, and equivalent response headers.
+- Other hosts, including the existing local static start command: configure equivalent response headers at the serving layer. `_headers` is not universally interpreted.
+
+CSP defaults to denying all resources; only same-origin images and styles are allowed. It prohibits scripts, network connections, forms, frames, workers, plugins, base URL changes, and framing by other sites. Referrer-Policy prevents outgoing referrer disclosure. Permissions-Policy denies unnecessary device APIs and browsing topics. Other headers enforce MIME checks, same-origin resource/opener isolation, disabled DNS prefetch, and HTTPS via HSTS (one year, without subdomain or preload commitments).
+
+A meta CSP and referrer policy also protect each page on hosts without custom header support. Meta cannot enforce frame-ancestors or replace HSTS, Permissions-Policy, or other HTTP-only headers. Deployment headers must therefore be configured; a successful source test does not prove a host applied them. These configurations have not been verified against a deployed endpoint. Confirm actual HTTPS response headers, including error responses, after deployment. Do not start a local server for these checks.
+
+References: [CSP specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP/), [Vercel configuration](https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/vercel-json).
+
+## Secure handling for future services
+
+No backend, personal-data store, account session, payment flow, or deletion API exists in this repository. Do not simulate one using browser storage. Before implementing those services:
+
+- Collect only fields needed for a stated purpose; keep optional marketing choices separate and off by default.
+- Validate input and authorization on the server, encode rendered output, and keep secrets and personal data out of bundles, URLs, analytics, and logs.
+- Use HTTPS, server-managed Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite session cookies, CSRF protection for mutations, and POST logout. Scope cookies narrowly; never store credentials or payment data in browser storage.
+- Define access controls, retention/deletion schedules, encrypted storage, and the process for data access/deletion requests. Configure host logs for the shortest necessary retention and restricted access; do not claim anonymous hosting or zero server logs without evidence.
+- Review any payment or ordering provider before integration and update the privacy notice before collecting data. Amend CSP narrowly for required functionality instead of enabling wildcards or unsafe-inline.
+
+The current source checks do not verify host settings, transport configuration, image licensing, or the security of future services.
